# Citation metadata for this repository (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
# Repository file only: nothing here is a published data release, and no DOI
# has been minted (standing decision of 2026-10-19: nothing is published or
# announced). GitHub renders this file as "Cite this repository".
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use CTAS or WorldsIndex in your work, cite this repository by its
  URL and the release date of the data you used (ctas/data/status.json
  generated_at, or the WorldsIndex release manifest). Every export carries the
  source credit lines of the providers it was built from; cite those sources
  as well.
type: software
title: "JackMcGuireAstro.github.io: CTAS and WorldsIndex"
abstract: >-
  Static research site hosting CTAS (the Cowboy Transient Alert System:
  a certified, source-complete aggregation of public transient and
  multimessenger records with per-source query receipts) and WorldsIndex (an
  exoplanet and host-star index with per-source identity states, conflict
  sets and transit ephemerides). Both are built every cycle by GitHub Actions
  and served as checksum-bound static files with IVOA-format exports (ECSV,
  VOTable 1.5, VOParquet, DataLink 1.1) and W3C PROV-JSON provenance.
authors:
  - family-names: McGuire
    given-names: Jack
    email: machoslothman@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/JackMcGuireAstro/JackMcGuireAstro.github.io"
url: "https://jackmcguireastro.github.io"
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - transients
  - multimessenger
  - exoplanets
  - virtual observatory
  - provenance
  - static site
date-released: "2026-10-19"
